# The working copy is LF on every platform. gofumpt treats a CRLF file as
# unformatted, so a checkout with core.autocrlf=true fails `make lint` and
# `make fmt-check` on every Go file at once; bash chokes on a CRLF script.
# text=auto leaves binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden recordings are compared byte for byte and hold ANSI escapes. Line
# endings must survive a checkout on Windows unchanged.
*.golden -text

# Recorded responses are what GitHub actually returned, and converting their
# line endings is a rewrite (.claude/rules/testing.md). Today's parsers do not
# mind, but a line-based one would then read different bytes here and on CI.
internal/gh/cli/testdata/** -text
